Chapter: EditHoleTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopEdit
  cites Works chapter GopFiles
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The Edit open's durable part inside a real D.5 hole of `desk-edit-want`
 bytes, the way `desk-edit-open` runs it: the GPT lookup bracketed at the
 frontier first, then `ged-build` inside the hole, then the exit and the
 claim. An overrun, a transient one included, would trap on the armed ceiling
 rather than print, so reaching the lines below is itself the fit; the room
 left is printed beside the verdict so the fit is a number.

 THE CONTROL IS THE FIRST LINE: an allocation taken before the hole is
 entered must not land in it, or the hole is only where allocations were
 going anyway. The buffer line reads the pointer `ged-ensure` parked, which
 must name memory inside the hole.

Section: Body

  eh-yn : Boolean -> Text
  eh-yn (v) = if v then "PASS" else "FAIL"

Section: Main

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing =
    let ms = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let es = alloc-zeroed 192 16
    in let block = alloc-zeroed desk-edit-want 64
    in let top = block + desk-edit-want
    in let push = desk-marks-push ms desk-focus-edit block
    in let kill = desk-marks-kill ms desk-focus-edit
    in let outside = alloc-bytes 64
    in let g0 = __heap-save
    in act
    start <- gpt-esp-start
    let r = __heap-restore g0
    in let f0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let i = desk-hole-enter ms top 0 desk-edit-want
    in act
    st <- ged-build start es
    let cur = alloc-bytes 0
    in let claimed = desk-hole-exit ms i desk-focus-edit
    in let f1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let buf = ged-buf es
    in act
    print-line-uni ("CONTROL, an allocation before the hole is outside it: " & eh-yn (outside < block | outside >= top))
    print-line-uni ("a dead span is picked: " & show i)
    print-line-uni ("the open allocated inside the hole: " & eh-yn (cur > block & cur < top))
    print-line-uni ("the buffer is inside the hole: " & eh-yn (buf >= block & buf + ged-cap <= top))
    print-line-uni ("room left " & show (top - cur) & ", at least a page: " & eh-yn (top - cur >= 4096))
    print-line-uni ("the frontier is unmoved: " & eh-yn (f1 == f0))
    print-line-uni ("the entry is claimed for Edit: " & eh-yn (desk-marks-id ms 0 == desk-focus-edit & desk-span-reusable ms 0 top 0 == False))
    print-line-uni ("the state is a listing of " & show (st.ed-count) & ": " & eh-yn (st.ed-mode == ged-mode-list & st.ed-count > 0))
    end
    end
    end